# Wendy Beauty & Spa — Website

Premium, mobile-first storefront for Wendy Beauty & Spa (wigs & hair, cosmetics,
beauty & spa services, women's fashion, shoes, skincare and accessories).

This is a **static site** — plain HTML/CSS/JS, no build step, no server required.
That means it deploys to Vercel in about two minutes, and you can push updates
straight from GitHub.

## What's included

- `index.html` — the full one-page site (header, hero, categories, shop, booking, about, team, contact, footer)
- `styles.css` — the design system (colors, type, layout)
- `script.js` — product catalogue, cart/wishlist (saved in the visitor's browser), search, WhatsApp links, booking form
- `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml` — basic SEO plumbing

## What's *not* built yet

This first version is the storefront **front end**. It does not yet include:
- A real backend, database, or payment gateway
- The admin dashboard (to edit products, prices, banners, bookings, etc. without touching code)
- Persisted orders/bookings (right now, "Add to Bag" and the booking form open a
  pre-filled WhatsApp message — nothing is charged or stored on a server)

When you're ready for that layer, the natural next step is Next.js + a database
(e.g. Supabase or Postgres) with an admin area, deployed the same way on Vercel.
Happy to build that next if you want it.

## Product data

All product info (names, descriptions, categories) lives in `script.js` in the
`PRODUCTS` array near the top. Every product currently has `price: null` and
`available: null`, which the site shows as **"PRICE ON REQUEST"** and
**"AVAILABILITY TO BE CONFIRMED"** — exactly as specified, so nothing is invented.
To set a real price, change `price: null` to `price: 25000` (for example).

## WhatsApp numbers

Both numbers are wired in as constants at the top of `script.js`:
```js
const WA1 = "2348137609506";
const WA2 = "2349012314878";
```
Update these in one place if the numbers ever change.

